 362+ 0412              ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
 363+ 0412              ; Unified guest memory interface
 364+ 0412              ;
 365+ 0412              ; Guest physical address is classified before selecting its physical backing:
 366+ 0412              ;   00000-9FFFF / C8000-FDFFF : guest RAM, pages 44h-83h
 367+ 0412              ;   A0000-BFFFF               : linear VGA aperture backing, pages 30h-37h
 368+ 0412              ;   C0000-C7FFF               : VGA BIOS slot, pages 20h-21h
 369+ 0412              ;   FE000-FFFFF               : system BIOS slot, page 10h (8 KiB image)
 370+ 0412              ;
 371+ 0412              ; The VGA aperture backend is deliberately a byte-linear staging layer over
 372+ 0412              ; the first 128 KiB of the 256 KiB VRAM allocation. It is NOT yet IBM VGA
 373+ 0412              ; plane/latch/read-mode/write-mode emulation. VGA register semantics are a
 374+ 0412              ; separate implementation stage.
 375+ 0412              ;
 376+ 0412              ; All backing is reached through WIN3. A is the page bias for the address
 377+ 0412              ; formula: page = (guest_high_nibble*4)+(guest_middle>>6)+bias.
 378+ 0412              ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
